    "result_text": "Full build passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` now follows `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and every value derived from it moves to the new identity. I touched only two small classes:\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds `Locality.region(owner) + \"-\" + hash8(...)`, where `hash8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized telephone (already E.164 at this pipeline stage) followed by the last name. Dropped the sequence logic and the `OwnerRepository` dependency entirely.\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 `locality(owner)` now returns the REGION segment of the owner's `customerCode` (splitting on the first `-`), falling back to the new public `region(owner)` helper (the former postcode-preferred / city-table derivation) only when no code is assigned yet.\n\nEverything else followed automatically because it already reads `customerCode`:\n- **membershipNumber** (`OwnerMapper`: `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy`)\n- **checkDigit** (`CheckDigit` runs Luhn over the digits in `customerCode`)\n- **audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated` logs `customerCode` \u2014 verified in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`)\n\nNo YAML, mapper, or other pipeline files needed changing. Test suite is green.",
